                        },
                        "description":"The Failure Root Causes resource manages the failure root causes. A failure root cause defines the underlying, originating causal factors that led to the occurrence of an asset failure event. Root causes represent the core causal factors, such as process, training, environment or design that are determined through a root cause analysis; in contrast, a cause code represents a technician-observed failure mechanism, such as rust, leak, rupture or shearing. More than one failure root cause may underly a single failure instance."
