                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey Finds shipment lines according to the shipment line number. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>ShipmentLine; integer;  Number that identifies the shipment line. </li></ul></li><li>findByShipment Finds shipment lines for the specified shipment. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>bindOrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inventory organization. </li><li>bindShipmentName; string;  Name of the shipment that's used for shipping goods to the destination location. </li></ul></li><li>findByShipmentAttributes Finds shipment lines based on specified shipment attributes. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>bindFromActualShipDate; string;  Start date of the date range for the shipment's actual ship date. </li><li>bindPackingSlipNumber; string;  Document that itemizes and describes the contents of the shipment. </li><li>bindPackingSlipStatus; string;  Indicates the state or condition of the packing slip. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup ORA_WSH_PACK_STATUS. </li><li>bindRcvShipmentNum; string;  Number identifying the advanced shipment notice from the supplier. </li><li>bindShipmentOrganizationId; integer;  Unique identifier for the inventory organization. </li><li>bindStatusCode; string;  Abbreviation indicating the state or condition of the shipment. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup type WSH_DELIVERY_STATUS. </li><li>bindToActualShipDate; string;  End date of the date range for the shipment's actual ship date. </li></ul></li></ul>",
