                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format: ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables:<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey :Find shipment line transaction requests according to the primary key criteria. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>TransactionId :Value that uniquely identifies the shipment line transaction request. </li></ul></li><li>findByLineAttributes :Find shipment line transaction requests according to line attributes. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>BaseItem :Name of the base item. </li><li>BaseItemId :Value that uniquely identifies the base Assemble to Order (ATO) model information used for internal processing. </li><li>Carrier :Name of the carrier that transports the shipment. </li><li>CarrierId :Value that uniquely identifies the carrier. </li><li>CarrierNumber :Number that identifies the carrier that transports the shipment. </li><li>EndAssemblyItem :Number that identifies the finished assembled item to build by using the item shipped on this shipment line. </li><li>FromRequestedDate :Initial date in a range corresponding to when the customer requested the order line. </li><li>FromScheduledShipDate :Initial date in a range corresponding to when the order line is scheduled to be shipped. </li><li>InitialDestinationId :Value that uniquely identifies the initial leg of the transportation planned to deliver the shipment to the final destination. </li><li>Item :Value that uniquely identifies the item. </li><li>ItemId :Value that uniquely identifies the inventory item. </li><li>ModeOfTransportCode :Abbreviation that identifies the mode of transport for the shipping method. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup WSH_MODE_OF_TRANSPORT. </li><li>OrderTypeCode :Abbreviation the identifies the type of source document. The default value is SALES_ORDER. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup ORA_WSH_ORDER_LINE_TYPE. </li><li>OrganizationCode :Abbreviation that identifies the ship-from organization. </li><li>OrganizationId :Value that uniquely identifies the inventory organization. </li><li>OrganizationName :Name of the inventory organization. </li><li>ServiceLevelCode :Abbreviation that identifies the service level for the shipping method. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup WSH_SERVICE_LEVELS. </li><li>ToRequestedDate :Final date in a range corresponding to when the customer requested the order line. </li><li>ToScheduledShipDate :Final date in a range corresponding to when the order line is scheduled to be shipped. </li><li>TransportationShipment :Value that identifies the planned shipment from the transportation management application. </li></ul></li></ul>",
