            "packingUnits-nestedPackingUnits-finder":{
                "name":"finder",
                "in":"query",
                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format: ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables:<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey :Finds packing unit according to the primary key. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>PackingUnitId :Value that uniquely identifies the packing unit. </li></ul></li><li>findAllLevelsByPackingUnit :Finds details of all levels of packing unit. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>pPackingUnit :Value that uniquely identifies the packing unit. </li></ul></li><li>findByCycleCount :Finds the counted or uncounted packing units in the subinventory or location for a cycle count. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>bindCOO :Abbreviation that identifies the country of origin. </li><li>bindCountedFlag :Value that indicates whether the packing units are counted or uncounted. If true, then packing units fetched are counted. If false, then the packing units fetched are uncounted. </li><li>bindCycleCountHeaderId :Value that uniquely identifies the cycle count. </li><li>bindItemId :Value that uniquely identifies the item. </li><li>bindLocatorId :Value that uniquely identifies the inventory locator. </li><li>bindLotNumber :Number that identifies a lot associated with one or more items. </li><li>bindOrgId :Value that uniquely identifies the organization. </li><li>bindOwningEntityId :Value that uniquely identifies the owning entity. If the item is consigned, this attribute contains the supplier site identifier. If the item is owned, it contains the owning organization identifier. </li><li>bindProjectId :Value that uniquely identifies the project. </li><li>bindRevision :Revision of the item. </li><li>bindSubinventory :Value that uniquely identifies the subinventory. </li><li>bindTaskId :Value that uniquely identifies the task. </li></ul></li><li>findByPhysicalInventory :Finds the counted or uncounted packing units in the subinventory or location for a physical inventory. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>bindCOO :Abbreviation that identifies the country of origin. </li><li>bindCountedFlag :Value that indicates whether the packing units are counted or uncounted. If true, the fetched packing units are counted. If false, the fetched packing units are uncounted. </li><li>bindItemId :Value that uniquely identifies the organization. </li><li>bindLocatorId :Value that uniquely identifies the inventory locator. </li><li>bindOrgId :Value that uniquely identifies the organization. </li><li>bindOwningEntityId :Value that uniquely identifies the owning entity. If the item is consigned, this attribute contains the supplier site identifier. If the item is owned, it contains the owning organization identifier. </li><li>bindPhysicalInventoryId :Value that uniquely identifies the physical inventory. </li><li>bindProjectId :Value that uniquely identifies the project. </li><li>bindRevision :Revision of the item. </li><li>bindSubinventory :Value that uniquely identifies the organization. </li><li>bindTaskId :Value that uniquely identifies the task. </li></ul></li><li>findByShipmentAndLineAttributes :Finds all packing units that match the specified criteria. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>LineStatusCodeValue :Abbreviation that identifies the status code of the shipment line. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup WSH_PICK_STATUS. </li><li>ShipmentIdValue :Value that uniquely identifies the shipment to which the packing unit's assigned. </li><li>SourceOrderIdValue :Value that uniquely identifies the source order header. </li></ul></li><li>findUnassignedOuterMostLPNs :Finds the outermost packing units that haven't been assigned to a shipment in an organization. <br>Finder Variables: <ul><li>bindOrganizationId :Value that uniquely identifies the organization. </li></ul></li></ul>",
                "required":false,
                "style":"form",
                "explode":true,
                "schema":{
                    "type":"string"
                },
                "x-adf-finder-formats":[
