            "inspectionEvents-finder":{
                "name":"finder",
                "in":"query",
                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey Finds the inspection event that matches the primary key criteria specified. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>IpEventId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inspection event. </li></ul></li><li>findInspectionEvents Finds the inspection event based on the criteria specified. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>bindAcceptanceQualityLimit; number;  Acceptance Quality Limit along with the Sample Size Code Letter is used to determine the sampling size. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup type ORA_QA_SAMPLING_AQL. </li><li>bindAssetId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the asset number to inspect if inspection type is Asset. </li><li>bindAssetNumber; string;  Alphanumeric value that identifies the asset number to inspect if inspection type is Asset. </li><li>bindCategoryId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the category of the item to inspect. </li><li>bindCategorySetId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the catalog of the item to inspect. </li><li>bindDocumentType; string;  Document type of the receiving inspection event. </li><li>bindEndDate; string;  Date and time on or before which the inspection event occurred. </li><li>bindEventType; string;  Abbreviation for the type of event. Valid values are WIP, RCV, INV, RES, or AST. </li><li>bindInspectedBy; string;  Person who performs the inspection. </li><li>bindInspectionLevelId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inspection level. </li><li>bindInspectionLevelName; string;  Name of the inspection level. </li><li>bindInspectionName; string;  Name of the inspection event. This attribute is derived from the event source. </li><li>bindInspectionPlanId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inspection plan. </li><li>bindInspectionPlanName; string;  Name of the inspection plan. </li><li>bindInspectionStatus; string;  Inspection status. Valid values include PENDING or COMPLETE. </li><li>bindInventoryItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inventory item to inspect. </li><li>bindItemNumber; string;  Number that identifies the item. </li><li>bindLotNumber; string;  Lot number inspected in this event. </li><li>bindOrganizationCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the list of values for the organization. </li><li>bindOrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the inventory organization. </li><li>bindOrganizationName; string;  Name of the organization. </li><li>bindQuantityRejected; number;  Total quantity rejected in this event. </li><li>bindReceiptNumber; string;  Receipt number that this inspection event inspects. </li><li>bindResourceCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the resource. </li><li>bindResourceId; integer;  Identifies the resource to inspect. </li><li>bindSamplingLevelCode; string;  Determines the relationship between the lot or batch size and the sample size. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup type ORA_QA_SAMPLING_INSP_LEVEL. </li><li>bindSamplingPlanType; string;  Code of the sampling plan type. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup type ORA_QA_SAMPLING_PLAN_TYPE. </li><li>bindSamplingStandardCode; string;  Sampling standard code associated with the inspection level. A list of accepted values is defined in the lookup type ORA_QA_SAMPLING_STD. </li><li>bindSourceOrganizationCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the source organization. This attribute is required when EventType is Receiving and DocumentType is In-transit shipment or Transfer order. </li><li>bindStartDate; string;  Date and time on or after which the inspection event occurred. </li><li>bindSubinventoryCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the subinventory that stores the inspected item. </li><li>bindSupplier; string;  Name of the supplier. This attribute is required when EventType is Receiving and DocumentType is Purchase order. </li><li>bindWorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area for a resource inspection. </li><li>bindWorkCenterCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the work center. </li><li>bindWorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center for a resource inspection. </li><li>bindWorkOrderId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order for a manufacturing inspection. </li><li>bindWorkOrderNumber; string;  Number that identifies the list of values for the work order. </li></ul></li><li>findSecuredInspectionEvents Finds inspection events based on the data privilege name specified. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>bindPrivilege; string;  Name of the data privilege. </li></ul></li></ul>",
