            "workOrders-finder":{
                "name":"finder",
                "in":"query",
                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey Finds work order details according to order identifier. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>WorkOrderId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderAndWorkAreaCenter Finds work orders that are planned to run in the work area or work center. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderB2BCM Finds work orders that include back-to-back processing or contract manufacturing. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>BackToBackFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y then the application created the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. If N then the application didn't create the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>ContractMfgFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then the application created the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. If N, then the application didn't create the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>InventoryItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the item, product, or assembly that the work order creates in the inventory organization. </li><li>ItemNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the item number. The user defines this number. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>PlannedCompletionDate; string;  Planned date and time to finish the work order. </li><li>PlannedStartDate; string;  Planned date and time to start the work order. </li><li>SourceHeaderRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkOrderId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByComponent Finds work orders that consume the component. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>BackToBackFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y then the application created the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. If N then the application didn't create the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>ContractMfgFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then the application created the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. If N, then the application didn't create the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. there's no default value for this attribute </li><li>FirmPlannedFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then prevent the planning system from suggesting changes to the work order. If N, then don't prevent. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>MaterialItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the item to issue in the inventory organization for the work order. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>PlannedCompletionDate; string;  Planned date and time to finish the work order. </li><li>PlannedStartDate; string;  Planned date and time to start the work order. </li><li>SourceHeaderRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByModifiedDate Finds work orders that include an updated date that occurs after the date that you specify. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>FirmPlannedFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then prevent the planning system from suggesting changes to the work order. If N, then don't prevent. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>InventoryItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the item, product, or assembly in the inventory organization that the work order creates. </li><li>LastUpdateDate; string;  Date when the user most recently modified the work order. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>SourceHeaderRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByResource Finds work orders that require the resource. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>BackToBackFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y then the application created the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. If N then the application didn't create the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>ContractMfgFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then the application created the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. If N, then the application didn't create the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. there's no default value for this attribute </li><li>FirmPlannedFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then prevent the planning system from suggesting changes to the work order. If N, then don't prevent. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>PlannedCompletionDate; string;  Planned date and time to finish the work order. </li><li>PlannedStartDate; string;  Planned date and time to start the work order. </li><li>ResourceId; integer;  Primary key that uniquely identifies the resource. Manufacturing generates this primary key when it creates the resource. </li><li>SourceHeaderRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderBySerial Finds work orders according to serial. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>BackToBackFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y then the application created the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. If N then the application didn't create the work order as part of a back-to-back flow. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>ContractMfgFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then the application created the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. If N, then the application didn't create the work order as part of the contract manufacturing flow. there's no default value for this attribute </li><li>FirmPlannedFlag; string;  Contains one of the following values Y or N. If Y, then prevent the planning system from suggesting changes to the work order. If N, then don't prevent. there's no default value for this attribute. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>PlannedCompletionDate; string;  Planned date and time to finish the work order. </li><li>PlannedStartDate; string;  Planned date and time to start the work order. </li><li>ProductSerialId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the assembly serial. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the serial number. </li><li>ResourceId; integer;  Primary key that uniquely identifies the resource. Manufacturing generates this primary key when it creates the resource. </li><li>SourceHeaderRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineRefId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderBySerialNumber Finds work orders according to serial number. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>SerialNumber; string;  Serial number that identifies the assembly that the work order creates. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByWorkAreaWorkCenter Finds work orders that the application plans to run in the work area or work center. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>InventoryItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the item, product, or assembly that the work order creates in the inventory organization. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>PlannedCompletionDate; string;  Planned date and time to finish the work order. </li><li>PlannedStartDate; string;  Planned date and time to start the work order. </li><li>SourceHeaderReferenceId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the header of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceLineReferenceId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the line of the document that represents the work order in the source system. </li><li>SourceSystemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the source system in the manufacturing cloud. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderStatusId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order status. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work order status. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByWorkDefinitionAndStartOperationSeq Finds impacted work orders based on the specified work definition and a newly added operation sequence. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>OperationSeqNumber; number;  Value that uniquely identifies the operation sequence in the work order to assess its impact on execution. </li><li>WorkDefinitionId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work definition of the work order to assess its impact on execution. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderByWorkOrderNumber Finds work orders according to work order number. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key generated by the application when the inventory organization is created. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrderSearch Finds work orders that are delayed. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersCompletingToday Finds work orders that must be finished today. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersDelayed Finds work orders that are delayed. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersOnHold Finds work orders that are on hold. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersOpDelayed Finds work orders that include delayed operations. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to operation. For example, if the tolerance is one hour, then only include each work order with an operation that's overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersStartingToday Finds work orders that the application plans to start today. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to time. For example, if Tolerance; integer;  is one hour, then only include work orders that are overdue according to one hour or more than one hour. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>WorkOrdersWithException Finds work orders that include an exception. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>DueDays; integer;  Finds work orders that are overdue according to days. For example, if DueDays; integer;  is 7, then only return each work order that includes an operation with a scheduled finish date that's greater than the current date minus 7 days. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies each inventory organization that's a manufacturing plant. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the inventory organization. </li><li>Tolerance; integer;  Finds exceptions that occur before the tolerance time limit expires. For example, if tolerance is 7 days, then the application won't include any exceptions that occur 7 days prior to the current date. </li><li>WorkAreaId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work area. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work area. </li><li>WorkCenterId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the work center. It's a primary key that the application generates when it creates the work center. </li><li>WorkOrderNumber; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the work order in the plant. </li></ul></li><li>findByProjectNumberTaskNumber Finds work order operations and dispatch statuses according to the project number and task number. This finder is associated with a feature that requires opt in. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>WoProjectNumber; string;  Number that identifies the project associated with the work order. This attribute is associated with a feature that requires opt in. </li><li>WoTaskNumber; string;  Number that identifies the task associated with the work order. This attribute is associated with a feature that requires opt in. </li></ul></li></ul>",
