            "relatedItemRelationships-finder":{
                "name":"finder",
                "in":"query",
                "description":"Used as a predefined finder to search the collection.<br><br>Format ?finder=&lt;finderName&gt;;&lt;variableName&gt;=&lt;variableValue&gt;,&lt;variableName2&gt;=&lt;variableValue2&gt;<br><br>The following are the available finder names and corresponding finder variables<br><br><ul><li>PrimaryKey Find related item relationships according to the primary key criteria. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>ItemRelationshipId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the related item relationship. </li></ul></li><li>findByOrganization Find related items according to the specified item and organization. The results will include master-controlled related items and related items that are applicable only to the specified organization. <br>Finder Variables <ul><li>FromInventoryItemId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the from item. </li><li>FromItem; string;  Value that uniquely identifies the from item in the related item relationship. </li><li>IncludeDerivedRelationships; boolean;  Value that indicates whether derived item relationships must be included in the response. The possible values are true and false. If the value for IncludeDerivedRelationships; boolean;  is true, then both the forward and derived items are returned in the response. If IncludeDerivedRelationships; boolean;  is null or false or the request doesn't have this finder variable, then only forward related item relationships are returned. </li><li>OrganizationCode; string;  Abbreviation that identifies the organization. </li><li>OrganizationId; integer;  Value that uniquely identifies the organization for which all the related items are to be fetched. </li></ul></li></ul>",
                "required":false,
